Do not re-check sessions that are waiting for their client when the settings are reread

When the broker rereads its settings (SIGHUP, which LiveQX sends after it
publishes a new certificate revocation list), mosquitto_security_apply_default()
walks every context, including persistent sessions whose client is offline.
With use_identity_as_username such a context has no TLS connection any more, so
it is disconnected "again" with the state forced back to "disconnecting".
context__disconnect() then runs a second time and puts the context into the
session expiry list a second time. The first entry is left pointing at the
context, which is freed later; session_expiry__check() then reads freed memory
and the broker dies with SIGSEGV (found with AddressSanitizer on 2.0.18; the
code is the same in 2.0.22).

Minimal reproduction: one MQTT 5 client connected with clean start off and a
session expiry interval above zero, disconnect it, send SIGHUP to the broker.

Two changes:
  * security_default.c: a context with no socket is skipped. There is nothing
    to re-check; it is judged when it connects (the code already says so for
    the per-listener branch: "Client not currently connected, so defer
    judgement until it does connect").
  * session_expiry.c: a context is in the list at most once, so the same
    mistake from any other path cannot leave a stale entry behind.

diff -ru a/src/security_default.c b/src/security_default.c
--- a/src/security_default.c	2023-09-19 00:29:34.000000000 +0300
+++ b/src/security_default.c	2026-10-23 13:43:41.353860745 +0300
@@ -1124,6 +1124,14 @@
 			continue;
 		}
 
+		if(context->sock == INVALID_SOCKET){
+			/* Not connected (a persistent session waiting for its client):
+			 * there is no certificate, user or listener state to re-check, and
+			 * disconnecting it again would add it to the session expiry list a
+			 * second time. It is judged when it connects. */
+			continue;
+		}
+
 		/* Check for anonymous clients when allow_anonymous is false */
 		if(db.config->per_listener_settings){
 			if(context->listener){
diff -ru a/src/session_expiry.c b/src/session_expiry.c
--- a/src/session_expiry.c	2023-09-19 00:29:34.000000000 +0300
+++ b/src/session_expiry.c	2026-10-23 13:43:41.353860745 +0300
@@ -75,6 +75,10 @@
 		}
 	}
 
+	/* A context is in the list at most once; a second entry would be left
+	 * pointing at the context after it is freed. */
+	session_expiry__remove(context);
+
 	item = mosquitto__calloc(1, sizeof(struct session_expiry_list));
 	if(!item) return MOSQ_ERR_NOMEM;
 
